 "description": "PRE-009 AI-assisted full-text extraction output, one report per call -- v1.1 (2026-10-09, D). Same 8 tables/row units as extract_schema_v1.json; fixes per 06_synthesis/prototype_2026-10-09/prototype_report.md (c)/(d) and T8_extraction_quality.csv: (a) dictionary-controlled fields that v1 left as free string (matrix, exercise_mode, design, training_status, clinical_endpoint) are now strict enums, each paired with an <field>_other_text free-text field used only when the enum's own 'other'/'other_*' value is chosen; time_unit is now a strict enum with no free-text pair (the dictionary's own boundary rules convert every reported unit to min/h/d, so no 'other' case exists); (b) analyte_id now separates analyte_raw (verbatim) from analyte_canonical (normalised; prompt rule list); (c) sample_sets time fields are restructured to time_text_raw (verbatim) + time_value_min (numeric minutes or null) + time_range_min ([lo,hi] minutes or null) + time_bin (unchanged enum), replacing timepoint_as_reported/time_from_exercise_end_value/time_unit; (d) precision_validation rows carry a required evidence_basis enum (stated_in_report/not_reported_in_report/not_applicable_to_design) whose relationship to evidence_state is stated in extract_prompt_v1_1.md (not machine-enforced here; Codex strict output schemas do not reliably support cross-field if/then). Still additionalProperties:false, every property required, no $ref/$defs/maxLength/uniqueItems.",
